cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the released artifacts, please cite the paper."
title: "HI-FTT: A Hospitality-Informed Feature-Tokenizer Transformer for Interpretable Hotel Booking-Cancellation Churn Prediction"
abstract: >-
  HI-FTT extends the FT-Transformer with two hospitality domain modules integrated
  into the forward pass: Booking-Phase Aware Conditioning (BPAC) and Semantic Group
  Attention (SGA), the latter producing a native CRM risk dashboard. Across five
  seeds HI-FTT significantly improves the vanilla FT-Transformer backbone on ROC-AUC
  and PR-AUC on the Hotel Booking Demand dataset (DeLong and paired-bootstrap tests),
  while gradient-boosted trees remain the strongest tabular baselines and the domain
  gain is shown to be hospitality-specific.
